{"qid":"Q1027","names":["Mauritius"],"title":"Mauritius","endonym":{"native":"République de Maurice","lang":"fr"},"capsule":"Mauritius (République de Maurice) is an island republic in the southwestern Indian Ocean, independent from Britain since 12 March 1968 and a republic since 12 March 1992. The economy diversified from sugar monoculture into textiles, tourism, and financial services under successive governments, making Mauritius one of Africa's highest per-capita-income states by the early 21st century. The country has pursued a longstanding sovereignty claim over the Chagos Archipelago (British Indian Ocean Territory), and in 2024 the United Kingdom agreed in principle to transfer sovereignty, though the agreement remained pending final ratification.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Mauritius's core island territories are unambiguously defined; the Chagos/BIOT sovereignty dispute means the outer boundary of claimed Mauritian territory is contested and legally unresolved.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Mauritius","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Mauritius"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Mauritius","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauritius"}],"britannica":"place/Mauritius","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Mauritius","rulers":[{"qid":"Q2166580","name":"Seewoosagur Ramgoolam","start":1968,"end":1982,"image":"Seewoosagur Ramgoolam.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Seewoosagur%20Ramgoolam.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"GPO","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q290061","name":"Veerasamy Ringadoo","start":1992,"end":199